WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.230
Now and again, you might stumble across an
entry in the SCP Foundation Archive that is

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:07.600
far more than meets the eye.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:13.120
As you are probably already aware, sometimes
the Foundation’s numerical SCP designations

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:19.230
can be referencing an entity, a creature,
an object, a location, or even a combination

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:23.430
of linked anomalies all sharing a version
of the same number.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:26.859
Such is partly the case with SCP-4812.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:34.220
In this instance, the designation number ‘4812’
doesn’t refer to one singular item or entity.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:41.390
Instead, it is more of a collective designation,
an umbrella term for three distinct, separate,

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:42.879
but connected anomalies.

00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:47.079
We’ve got a lot of ground to cover here,
so without further ado, let’s take a look

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:52.150
at SCP-4812, better known collectively as
‘Wrath’.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:56.109
We’ll begin in a cavern deep beneath Alès,
in the south of France,

00:00:56.109 --> 00:01:02.590
where we find the first of the entities to
share the designation SCP-4812.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:10.730
This creature, large and without its own distinct
form, is referred to as SCP-4812-S. It possesses

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:15.820
a number of long appendages that protrude
from its amorphous body, each one covered

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:19.579
in a sticky, adhesive, a sort of glue-like
substance.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:25.630
In addition, each appendage, as well as the
rest of SCP-4812-S’ body, is covered in

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:33.320
fine hair that is hydrophobic, meaning that
it does not absorb water, and in fact, actively

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.760
repels it.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:40.790
These tendrils extend deep into the walls
of the cavern surrounding the creature.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:46.369
SCP-4812-S also has an inherent, latent ability
to affect anyone that visually perceives it.

00:01:46.369 --> 00:01:49.930
In other words, look upon this creature at
your own peril.

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:53.330
And we don’t mean that looking at it will
drive you mad.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:57.920
The fact is that nobody has been able to look
directly at this creature without suffering

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.680
a horrific, grizzly death.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:07.190
Upon taking even the quickest glimpse at SCP-4812-S,
the person observing will suffer the same

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:12.220
effect they would if their eyes, brain, and
entire nervous system had been dipped in caustic

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:13.220
acid.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:18.850
Yes, this creature instantly melts down on
a molecular level anyone who is brave enough

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:22.000
or foolish enough to look directly at it.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.950
That means a pain unlike any you could imagine,
bleeding through the skin and all orifices,

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:32.750
paralysis, asphyxiation, and then death, in
that order.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:37.120
Humans cannot directly interact with the creature
unless it is submerged in total darkness,

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.650
where they cannot perceive it visually.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:45.890
The anomalous hazard of this entity even extends
to photos or video recordings of SCP-4812-S.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:51.510
However, the effect is not as immediate or
violent when someone just looks at an image

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.960
or video of it.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:56.940
Still, you might want to check that your brain
isn’t melting after this video’s over

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.520
- just to be safe.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:06.170
Beyond killing anyone that sees it, SCP-4812-S
does very little, staying quite still in its

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:11.370
cave behind the maximum security doors the
Foundation has put in place at the entrance.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.980
So, that’s our first of the SCP-4812s.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:16.040
Who’s next?

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:22.750
How about SCP-4812-E, an approximately fifteen-meter-tall
humanoid made of platinum?

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:27.730
This entity appears vaguely skeletal, with
traces of tungsten and other metal compounds

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.850
in its composition.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:38.840
SCP-4812-E remains at a constant body temperature
of 0.0000000031 Kelvin or almost negative

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.140
460 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:46.730
However, this entity can also absorb the heat
around it without changing its own temperature,

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:51.890
reducing a cell at room temperature to absolute
zero in around sixteen seconds flat.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:57.850
And it’s because of this that SCP-4812-E
is often surrounded by a layer of frozen air

00:03:57.850 --> 00:03:59.110
and water.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:05.160
Much like the other creature it shares a designation
with, close interactions with SCP-4812-E are

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.660
often deadly.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:11.530
Stand too close, and the air around you would
drop in temperature rapidly, the water within

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:16.070
your body would freeze, and in seconds you
would die.

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:20.440
Even with the use of a specially insulated
suit, you would be lucky to gain a few short

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.420
moments of added protection.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:28.520
The only thing that weakens SCP-4812-E’s
effect is to expose it to extreme heat, although

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:33.480
this does not stop the temperature absorption
entirely, just slows it.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.390
But it’s through the constant application
of high temperatures that the Foundation has

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:43.370
been able to keep SCP-4812-E contained in
a thermally controlled vault kept intensely

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:45.250
hot at all times.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:52.890
Finally, we have the last of the three, designated
as SCP-4812-K, and we recommend anyone with

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.550
a bug phobia to look away now.

00:04:55.550 --> 00:05:00.690
This creature is an enormous winged insect,
almost like a cross between a stag beetle

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:04.380
and a scorpion in some of the physical traits
it shares with them.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:10.490
While its size might be significantly bigger,
measuring 180 meters long, the insect possesses

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:16.760
two large pincers, four legs, four wings that
extend from its back, and a long, segmented

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:19.490
tail with a pointed barb at the tip.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:24.180
Yes, this creepy-crawly would need a lot more
than just a can of Raid to get rid of it.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:31.940
But perhaps most strangely of all is SCP-4812-K’s
face, not the typical insect eyes and mouth

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:36.210
you would expect, but the face of a human
male.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:41.760
Much like its cavern dwelling counterpart,
SCP-4812-K tends to not do all that much when

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:42.760
left alone.

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:47.210
It can usually be found flying through the
upper stratosphere, only really moving when

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:48.910
it flaps its wings.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:53.240
You might have a hard time trying to spot
it, though, as its body is coated in reflective

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:54.240
chitin.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:59.880
In other words, the bug’s exoskeleton refracts
light away from it and makes it almost invisible.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.700
While the SCP Foundation has made attempts
to secure and contain this gigantic flying

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:09.430
insect after they learned of its existence,
the creature’s sheer size and strength have

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:13.280
destroyed any fighter jets or drones they
have sent after it.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:18.410
It seems impervious to damage from conventional
weapons, with anything fired at it being almost

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:22.100
perfectly reflected and directed back towards
the shooter.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:28.440
All the Foundation can really do is hope that
nobody else spots it and keep a close eye

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.040
on SCP-4812-K through regular surveillance.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:36.450
Above all, though, one procedure remains consistent
and of the utmost importance with every aspect

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:43.530
of SCP-4812: Never, under any circumstances,
can any of them be allowed to interact with

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:44.570
the other two.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.790
So, what could possibly connect these three
creatures?

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:52.690
An amorphous entity that kills anyone who
looks at it, a giant humanoid made of platinum

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:57.830
that alters temperature without absorbing
heat, and a winged insect that is almost perfect

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.889
at reflecting anything around it.

00:06:59.889 --> 00:07:02.210
They all seem to be pretty disconnected.

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:08.870
Yet, their common thread must be pretty significant
for all three to share the title of SCP-4812.

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:14.070
Indeed if they had no relation to each other,
they could each have their own unique number.

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:20.580
And what is the mysterious fourth, redacted
entity that is also referred to as SCP-4812?

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:24.180
The answers to this multitude of questions
aren’t exactly straightforward.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:28.680
Still, there does exist a series of anomalous
documents and items that the Foundation has

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:32.420
recovered that feature some of the necessary
information.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:37.440
Recovered from Markus de Wees, a Dutch collector
of anomalous artifacts, these items are referred

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:43.350
to as The Connington Set, named after Winston
J. Connington, an English archaeologist and

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:48.830
occultist whose research led the Foundation
to the discovery of a number of SCPs.

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:54.350
Among the various artifacts of The Connington
Set is a journal kept by Connington himself,

00:07:54.350 --> 00:08:00.060
featuring depictions of the different SCP-4812
creatures and notes recording his findings.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:04.750
The Set also features three hefty tomes written
in German over the course of many years that

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.710
contain multiple archaic coordinates.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:13.800
In one, an addition in Italian by another
author seems to shed a little light on SCP-4812.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:19.520
The translation of this section tells of an
ancient kingdom, respected above all others.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:23.831
Known either as the ‘House of Apollyon’,
or the ‘Sky Kings of Old Europ’, the first

00:08:23.831 --> 00:08:30.260
ruler of this kingdom was allegedly a descendant
of the King of Crimson Skies, or Asem the

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:31.350
First Man.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:36.479
These Sky Kings ruled over what is now modern-day
Europe for a hundred generations, conquering

00:08:36.479 --> 00:08:38.290
all who opposed them.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:43.630
Among their adversaries were “those faithful
to the iron god”, presumably the Mekhanites,

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:48.330
the ancient machine-worshipping religion that
preceded The Church of the Broken God.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:53.880
Eventually, however, complacency reared its
ugly head, and Sky King Sarrus VIII von Apollyon

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:58.200
looked beyond the realms of men, hoping to
find new land to conquer.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:04.000
Sarrus VIII assembled his forces, the largest
army ever seen, and set his sights on the

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:08.650
lands of the Fair Folk, more commonly known
as fairies nowadays.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:13.190
These Fair Folk were already engaged in conflict
with their southern neighbors, the Children

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:18.480
of the Moon, and were drastically underprepared
for Sarrus’ approaching forces.

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:22.560
Within two weeks, the fairies were scattered,
driven from their lands.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:27.990
There was, however, a sole survivor, a fae
princess, who was captured and faced the grim

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:30.520
fate of being taken as a trophy.

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:32.470
But the princess had other plans.

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:37.180
While being taken back to the Sky King’s
domain, she cast a curse upon the House of

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.820
Apollyon, and Sarrus VIII in particular.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:45.160
A horrific storm swept the returning ships
as the fae princess prayed to an ancient,

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:48.670
nameless god for vengeance against her peoples’
conquerors.

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:53.480
According to legend, the chains that had her
shackled to Sarrus’ ship caught fire, and

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:56.970
the blaze spread until it had burned the Sky
King’s ship to ash.

00:09:56.970 --> 00:10:01.780
It has even been said that the same chains
then wrapped around Sarrus himself, dragging

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:04.140
him down into the ocean’s depths.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:09.970
Then, to defend against any further dark magic
from the remaining Fair Folk, Sarrus IX appointed

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:12.540
four knights to defend his kingdom.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:16.160
By now, you might still be wondering what
any of this has to do with SCP-4812.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:20.339
But don’t worry, we’re getting there,
we promise.

00:10:20.339 --> 00:10:25.620
So, as the story continues, the remaining
ships were still able to bring the fae princess

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:30.830
back, and she was brought before Sarrus’
heir, Sarrus IX von Apollyon, who imprisoned

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:32.670
her for what she had done.

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:36.490
The princess was sent to a sealed dungeon
deep beneath the oceans.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:41.930
This prison is heavily implied to be the first
of the SCP-4812 entities, better known to

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:48.470
us as SCP-4812-S. However, the explanations
of the heatsink platinum humanoid and the

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:53.140
reflective flying insect are a little harder
to decipher from Winston J Connington’s

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:54.140
journal.

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:56.760
While most of Connington’s notes are written
in a cipher,

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:59.430
a few sections have been translated.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:03.830
According to him, from her prison deep below
the Earth, the voice of the fairy princess

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:08.630
was able to communicate with the souls of
the four knights protecting Sarrus IX’s

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:09.630
kingdom.

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:14.200
As a result, the Sky King was forced to banish
them, and this brought forth what Connington

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:17.230
referred to as ‘the great profanities’.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:21.960
Without the knights’ defense, some force
known as the Vinuvinex, the first profanity,

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:26.510
was able to cast its ‘cold hand’ over
Sarrus’ only daughter, killing her.

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:29.860
A creature whose very presence can drain the
heat from a person?

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:33.450
Sounds an awful lot like SCP-4812-E, huh?

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:37.920
In retaliation for his daughter’s death,
Sarrus drew up an ancient spear called the

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:43.440
Godless Lance and struck the being down, casting
it into the Earth’s molten core and subduing

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:47.690
SCP-4812-E with the intense heat below.

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:52.279
Another section describes ‘The King of Many
Faces’, Lamenellant, the creature we know

00:11:52.279 --> 00:11:59.260
as SCP-4812-K. Connington’s findings describe
this entity’s slaughter of the Daeva, a

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:00.600
neighboring kingdom.

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:05.459
The enormous insect appeared from the ‘the
space beyond spaces’ and would deflect perfectly

00:12:05.459 --> 00:12:10.450
any attack made against it, before taking
the faces of the Daeva and returning to the

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:11.450
skies.

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:16.940
But there was one final profanity, known only
as the Profane Dark.

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:22.310
The legend concludes with this profanity,
a dark, black smear, rising from the graves

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:23.830
of the Fair Folk.

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:28.310
It soaked through the earth and burst from
below, claiming the Sky King and dragging

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:30.420
him into an endless void.

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:35.399
As it pulled him away, Sarrus cursed the Profane
Dark, calling it ‘YASH’, the last great

00:12:35.399 --> 00:12:36.960
foe of man.

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:41.640
Watching his kingdom fall without the protection
of his four knights, all the Sky King could

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:44.880
utter was one repeated word:
“Wrath…Wrath, wrath, wrath.”

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:50.860
Now go check out “SCP-1461 - House of the
Worm” and “SCP-5000 Why?

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:56.070
- The Full Story Compilation” for more wild
stories from the universe of the SCP Foundation!

